import orchestrate as team
team.JOBS={
 'live-updates': '''Create ONLY dist/live.js and dist/version.json. Implement browser live engine swapping without page reloads. Contract coordinator will implement: game.js ES module exports synchronous mount(transfer=null), returns { capture(), dispose(), pause?(), resume?() }; capture returns a transferable in-memory object including world, positions, peer/conn objects, role/network flags, active tool, renderer (reused), hook state, elapsed and view. dispose stops RAF/event listeners and disposes OLD scene but MUST NOT destroy shared peer/conn or renderer. mount creates new scene and uses transferred shared objects; may throw. live.js is only initial script entry, loads version.json cache:no-store, then import('./game.js?build='+build), calls mount(null). Poll version.json every 6 seconds (when visible; visibilitychange check), backoff errors (silent network errors should not disrupt play). On changed build, import new module first while old engine keeps running, fetch new CSS before swap, capture old engine latest state, pause old if method exists, then call newModule.mount(transfer), dispose old only after success, set new engine and build. Catch import/mount failure: old.resume() if paused; keep old game and show small nonblocking #updateStatus message 'Update paused — still playing this version'; retry only on a DIFFERENT manifest build or after 60sec. No location.reload, no WebRTC disconnect, no save wipes. Shared hook instance is allowed to finish in old implementation. THREE static imported modules cache: coordinator will add build query strings on imports during packaging, so do not rewrite module source. version.json schema {build:'initial-1',protocol:1}; if protocol differs from initial, do not hot-swap, show 'An update is ready for your next session' (avoid incompatible multiplayer). During successful update show small 'Ocean updated. Keep playing.' toast #updateStatus auto-hide. Add own small CSS via JS for #updateStatus independent of game CSS, use system font, navy/cream no emoji. CSS assets style.css, graphics.css updated by staged <link> elements with ?build= token, load all before activation (media=print trick; onload switch). Do not rewrite body/index HTML automatically because engine DOM IDs must stay stable; live game logic may refresh dynamic elements on mount. Keep old links until staged loaded. Output window.raftLive read-only getters {build, updating,lastError} plus check() callable (for QA; invokes actual manifest check no cheats). Default initial import failure show a useful visible error card and console.error. Clear interval on pagehide? pagehide doesn't need stop engine except bfcache support. NO shell, git, deployments or further agents. Only live.js/version.json. Return exact API and limitations including shell HTML changes require next session unless existing elements can be updated by mount.'''
}
team.launch()
